Natural Earth: terms of use
===========================

Source: https://www.naturalearthdata.com/about/terms-of-use/ (read 2026-10-06)

The data in this dataset is Natural Earth's, and Natural Earth places it in
the public domain. Its terms of use, quoted as published:

  All versions of Natural Earth raster + vector map data found on this
  website are in the public domain. You may use the maps in any manner,
  including modifying the content and design, electronic dissemination, and
  offset printing. The primary authors, Tom Patterson and Nathaniel Vaughn
  Kelso, and all other contributors renounce all financial claim to the maps
  and invites you to use them for personal, educational, and commercial
  purposes.

  No permission is needed to use Natural Earth. Crediting the authors is
  unnecessary.

  However, if you wish to cite the map data, simply use one of the following.

  Short text:
  Made with Natural Earth.

  Long text:
  Made with Natural Earth. Free vector and raster map data @
  naturalearthdata.com.

  [...]

  The authors provide Natural Earth as a public service and are not
  responsible for any problems relating to accuracy, content, design, and
  how it is used.

Third-party data credited on the same page
------------------------------------------

The page names four providers, each with a release of the same form:
"Natural Earth is hereby granted a non-exclusive license to use the data
being provided by <provider> for the sole purpose of creating a world base
map", followed by a disclaimer of completeness, accuracy and fitness.

  - The Washington Post (no theme stated)
  - European Commission, Joint Research Centre, Institute for Environment and
    Sustainability (JRC IES): river and lake data, for Europe only
  - XNR Productions: road transportation data, for North America only
  - International Mapping Associates, Inc.: time zone data

It also says: "The authors' used name data for more than 20 languages from
Wikidata which is under a CC0 (public domain) license."

These are licences granted to Natural Earth. Natural Earth distributes the
whole of its data as public domain; how far that statement covers the parts
derived from these providers is not something the page settles. Users with
that concern should read the page themselves.

What this copy changes
----------------------

raw/: the publisher's zips, byte for byte.

parquet/: one GeoParquet file per layer, made from the shapefile in its zip.
All attribute fields are kept under their names and in their order, typed
from the .dbf field definitions; text decoded in the layer's encoding and
written as UTF-8; empty text, numbers and dates as NULL. Geometry unchanged
(no reprojection, no repair), in EPSG:4326 longitude/latitude as stated in
the .prj. Not an endorsement by Natural Earth.

The scripts that made this copy are MIT licensed:
https://github.com/yuiseki/natural-earth
